SUMMARY (non-binding; sections 1-11 govern)

    The Software is proprietary. You may READ it, RUN it, TEST it, and PUBLISH
    what you find — including criticism, benchmarks, and audit findings. You may
    NOT deploy it, sell it, redistribute it, or build a product on it. Those
    rights require a separate written licence.


1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means this repository and all source code, documentation,
    configuration, scenario, data, and model files it contains.

1.2 "Owner" means the copyright holder identified above.

1.3 "You" means any person or entity exercising the grant in section 3.

1.4 "Evaluation Purpose" means any of the following, whether performed for
    yourself or on behalf of another party:

    (a) technical, financial, or model evaluation, review, or verification;
    (b) audit, including independent model audit and model-risk review;
    (c) due diligence conducted by or for a prospective lender, investor,
        development finance institution, counterparty, or regulator;
    (d) academic research and teaching;
    (e) journalism and public-interest reporting;
    (f) security research and vulnerability disclosure;
    (g) benchmarking against other models or tools.

    Evaluation Purpose does NOT include production use, commercial exploitation,
    or use of the Software to model, price, or transact a real project other than
    for the purpose of reviewing this Software itself.

1.5 "Findings" means analyses, reviews, critiques, benchmark results, audit
    reports, academic publications, and security disclosures ABOUT the Software.


2. RESERVATION OF RIGHTS

    The Software is the confidential and proprietary property of the Owner. All
    rights not expressly granted in section 3 are reserved. The publication or
    public visibility of this repository does not grant any licence, express or
    implied, beyond the grant in section 3.


3. EVALUATION, AUDIT AND DUE DILIGENCE GRANT

    Subject to sections 5 through 7, the Owner grants You a non-exclusive,
    worldwide, royalty-free, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable
    licence to, solely for an Evaluation Purpose:

    3.1 access, view, download, and make copies of the Software;

    3.2 execute and test the Software, including against Your own inputs and
        scenarios;

    3.3 modify the Software locally to the extent reasonably necessary to conduct
        the evaluation — for example to instrument it, patch it, isolate a
        behaviour, or reproduce a defect; and

    3.4 disclose the Software to Your own employees, contractors, and
        professional advisers who are engaged in the same Evaluation Purpose and
        who are bound by terms no less restrictive than these.


4. PUBLICATION OF FINDINGS

    You may publish and distribute Findings without seeking the Owner's approval,
    and the Owner will not withhold or condition the grant in section 3 on the
    content of Findings. Findings may quote or reproduce excerpts of the Software
    to the extent reasonably necessary to substantiate a statement made — for
    example a function, a configuration block, or a computed result.

    This section does not permit publication of the Software in whole, or of
    excerpts so extensive that they substitute for access to the Software.

    A Findings publication should identify the version or commit examined.

    The rights in this section survive revocation under section 7 in respect of
    Findings already published, and in respect of Findings substantially prepared
    before revocation took effect.


5. RESTRICTIONS

    Except under a separate written licence from the Owner, You may NOT:

    5.1 use the Software in production, or to provide any commercial service, or
